      "message": "fix(import): refuse a STEP item whose context states no angle unit in a degree file\n\nUnlistedAngles judged only items with no unit context. An item whose\ncontext states no plane angle unit also takes the default units, so the\nreader reads its angles in radians. In a file that states degrees\nelsewhere, that item had wrong geometry without a word.\n\nUnlistedAngles now keeps each item's context by the reader's rules and\nthe contexts that state a plane angle unit. It refuses by name an item\nwith no context or with a context that states no angle unit, when the\nfile states an angle unit that is not the radian. This is the same\nshape as the length rule of #2919.\n\nPins (crates/kernel/tests/step_short_units.rs):\n- item_in_a_context_with_no_angle_unit_in_a_degree_file_is_refused_by_name\n- item_in_a_context_with_no_angle_unit_in_a_radian_file_is_kept (control)\n\nRefs #3079\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
